# Instructions

Audit only the current target decision identified by checks. Neighboring pages are read-only context; their independent errors do not invalidate the target. Do not proofread typos, calculate formulas, judge author opinions, invent absent text or audit final heading levels. FAIL requires a concrete, locatable error repairable through ownership, continuation or an existing reference relationship. Vague suspicion is not an error.

Audit continues_from_previous for the current footnote text block: whether it belongs to the same natural paragraph as its genuine footnote predecessor. Body and footnotes are independent streams. Page numbers, main text and publisher directions cannot serve as a footnote predecessor.

One footnote may contain several natural paragraphs, so sharing a citation ID does not require joining. Two distinct new notes must be separate. Join blocks splitting one word or an unfinished syntactic construction; keep independent new paragraphs separate. A standalone formula is a hard boundary; an image or table alone does not force a break.

# True

The specified existing structural decision is valid, or the evidence is insufficient to require correction.

# False

The specified decision has a clear, locatable and structurally repairable error.
